<div class="byblos-docs-article">

    <h1>{{#str}}docs_topic_pedagogy, local_byblos{{/str}}</h1>
    <p class="byblos-docs-lead">
        A portfolio is not a folder of files. Done well, it is one of the most powerful things a learner
        can do, which is why the Association of American Colleges &amp; Universities
        (AAC&amp;U) names the
        ePortfolio a <strong>high-impact educational practice</strong>. This page explains the ideas that make
        portfolios work, and how Byblos is built around them. The
        <a href="{{{links.best_practices}}}">Best practices</a> page turns these ideas into concrete advice.
    </p>

    <h2>More than storage: create, collect, curate, connect, and reflect</h2>
    <p>
        An ePortfolio gives learners a space to <strong>create, collect, curate and connect</strong> their
        academic experiences, and to write reflectively about them (Ohio State University, no date a). Its real
        job is to help students "connect the dots" across a curriculum that is otherwise experienced as
        separate, disconnected courses, making learning visible and turning a pile of work into a story
        about a person who is learning.
    </p>

